  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "in every century, there is a chosen one. Therefore, we do not live in a society\n--Last paragraphs of the IZhO 2022 Editorial\n\nK0Kalaru47 was out with his friends and he started to tell them about a CP Task. Because the statement was informal, his friends quickly parried with \"Who Asked\", so here is the formal statement:\n\nGiven arrays PPP and CCC of size (N+K)(N+K)(N+K) each, the beauty of an array BBB of size (N+K)(N+K)(N+K) is defined as the sum of CiC_iCi​ for all 1≤i≤(N+K)1\\leq i \\leq (N+K)1≤i≤(N+K) such that Bi=PiB_i = P_iBi​=Pi​.\n\nMore formally, the beauty of an array BBB is equal to ∑i=1∣B∣Ci\\large\\sum^{|B|}_{i=1} C_i∑i=1∣B∣​Ci​ [Bi=Pi][B_i = P_i][Bi​=Pi​]\n\nGiven an array AAA of size NNN such that (1≤Ai≤M)(1 \\leq A_i \\leq M)(1≤Ai​≤M).\nYour task is to insert KKK elements into the array such that:\n\n\nEach inserted element lies in the range [1,M][1, M][1,M].\nThe beauty of the final array is **maximized**.\nNote that, an element can be inserted at any index of the array.\n\nYou should find two values:\n\n\nThe **maximum** beauty that can be obtained across all arrays of size (N+K)(N+K)(N+K).\nThe **number of distinct arrays** of size (N+K)(N+K)(N+K) having the maximum beauty. Note that, two arrays XXX and YYY are said to be different if there exists some index iii such that Xi≠YiX_i ≠ Y_iXi​=Yi​. Since the number of distinct arrays can be huge, print the value modulo MODMODMOD.\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input consists of 444 integers N,K,MN,K,MN,K,M and MODMODMOD\nThe second line of input contains NNN space-separated integers - the array AAA.\nThe third line of input contains (N+K)(N+K)(N+K) space-separated integers - the array PPP.\nThe fourth line of input contains (N+K)(N+K)(N+K) space-separated integers - the array CCC.\n\n\nOutput Format\nPrint two integers separated by a single space.\n\n\n\nThe first integer corresponds to the **maximum** beauty that can be obtained across all arrays of size (N+K)(N+K)(N+K).\nThe second integer corresponds to the **number of distinct arrays** of size (N+K)(N+K)(N+K) having the maximum beauty. Since the number of distinct arrays can be huge, print the value modulo MODMODMOD.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤N,K≤20001 \\le N,K \\le 20001≤N,K≤2000",
      "1≤M≤1091 \\le M \\le 10^91≤M≤109",
      "2≤MOD≤1092 \\le MOD \\le 10^92≤MOD≤109",
      "1≤Ai,Pi≤M1 \\le A_i,P_i \\le M1≤Ai​,Pi​≤M",
      "−109≤Ci≤109-10^9 \\le C_i \\le 10^9−109≤Ci​≤109",
      "Subtasks",
      "**Subtask 1 (100 points):** Original constraints."
    ],
